{
  "id": "COMPOUND:36711 - PROTEIN:6340",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a potential mechanism by which the compound [(3R,4R,5R,6S)-6-[[(1S,2S,5R,7S,10R,12S,15R,16R,17S,18R,21R,22S,24S)-21,22-dihydroxy-1,6,6,15,17,20,20-heptamethyl-19,23-dioxaheptacyclo[13.10.0.02,12.05,10.010,12.016,24.018,22]pentacosan-7-yl]oxy]-4,5-dihydroxyoxan-3-yl] acetate interacts with the EZH2/SUZ12/EED complex. This compound is linked to the CD70 antigen, which is a known target of several molecules, including Azelate. The CD70 antigen is involved in immune signaling, and its interaction with EZH2/SUZ12/EED complex may influence gene expression through histone methylation. The evidence suggests that the compound may modulate the activity of the EZH2 complex, potentially affecting gene regulation in a biological context. The mechanism is supported by the presence of multiple pathways converging on the CD70 antigen and its interaction with the EZH2 complex, though the exact mode of action remains to be fully elucidated.",
